{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Python 3 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Python 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n# coding: utf-8\n\n# Read input\nline = input().strip().split()\nn = int(line[0])\nh = int(line[1])\n\n# Initialize DP table\nMAX_N = 36\nheight_dp = [[0] * MAX_N for _ in range(MAX_N)]\nheight_dp[0][0] = 1\n\n# Fill the DP table using recursive relation for binary trees\nfor node_count in range(1, MAX_N):\n    for min_height in range(node_count + 1):\n        count = 0\n        for root in range(1, node_count + 1):\n            left_size = root - 1\n            right_size = node_count - root\n            \n            # Compute valid configurations\n            left_full = height_dp[left_size][0]\n            right_full = height_dp[right_size][0]\n            left_below = height_dp[left_size][max(min_height - 1, 0)]\n            right_below = height_dp[right_size][max(min_height - 1, 0)]\n            \n            count += left_full * right_full - (left_full - left_below) * (right_full - right_below)\n        \n        height_dp[node_count][min_height] = count\n\nprint(height_dp[n][h])\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <string>\n\nint main() {\n    std::string line;\n    std::getline(std::cin, line);\n    line = line.erase(0, line.find_first_not_of(\" \\t\\r\\n\"));\n    line = line.erase(line.find_last_not_of(\" \\t\\r\\n\") + 1);\n    \n    std::vector<std::string> tokens;\n    size_t start = 0;\n    size_t end = line.find(' ');\n    while (end != std::string::npos) {\n        tokens.push_back(line.substr(start, end - start));\n        start = end + 1;\n        end = line.find(' ', start);\n    }\n    tokens.push_back(line.substr(start));\n    \n    int n = std::stoi(tokens[0]);\n    int h = std::stoi(tokens[1]);\n    \n    const int MAX_N = 36;\n    std::vector<std::vector<long long>> height_dp(MAX_N, std::vector<long long>(MAX_N, 0));\n    height_dp[0][0] = 1;\n    \n    for (int node_count = 1; node_count < MAX_N; node_count++) {\n        for (int min_height = 0; min_height <= node_count; min_height++) {\n            long long count = 0;\n            for (int root = 1; root <= node_count; root++) {\n                int left_size = root - 1;\n                int right_size = node_count - root;\n                \n                long long left_full = height_dp[left_size][0];\n                long long right_full = height_dp[right_size][0];\n                long long left_below = height_dp[left_size][std::max(min_height - 1, 0)];\n                long long right_below = height_dp[right_size][std::max(min_height - 1, 0)];\n                \n                count += left_full * right_full - (left_full - left_below) * (right_full - right_below);\n            }\n            height_dp[node_count][min_height] = count;\n        }\n    }\n    \n    std::cout << height_dp[n][h] << std::endl;\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-6.782778655178845e-05, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -2.3841855067985307